@startuml

title 11. Status history, audit fields and deletion rules

hide circle
skinparam linetype ortho

enum StatusHistoryEntityType {
	order
	purchase
	inventory_document
	production_order
	payment
}

entity StatusHistory {
	* id: int
	--
	* entityType: StatusHistoryEntityType
	* entityId: int
	fromStatus: string(255)?
	* toStatus: string(255)
	comment: text?
	* changedAt: DateTimeImmutable
	* store: Store
	changedBy: User?
}

Store ||--o{ StatusHistory : has status logs
User |o--o{ StatusHistory : changes status
StatusHistoryEntityType ||--o{ StatusHistory : classifies

note right of StatusHistory
  Current project status:
  - StatusHistory is not implemented.
  - Many entities already have status fields and audit columns.
  - Status changes are not logged centrally.

  Required behavior:
  - Every business status transition should create a history row.
  - History stores entity type and entity id to avoid hard coupling.
  - History rows are append-only.
  - UI should show history on Order, Purchase,
    InventoryDocument, ProductionOrder and Payment pages.
end note

note bottom
  Shared deletion/audit policy:

  Soft delete:
  - Product, Category, Unit, Warehouse, Customer, Supplier,
    ProductPrice, Payment and other user-managed dictionaries
    should use deletedAt where historical rows depend on them.

  Hard delete:
  - Draft documents can usually be hard deleted
    if they have no posted movements/payments.

  Never hard delete:
  - Posted InventoryDocument
  - StockMovement
  - Payment with accounting impact
  - StatusHistory

  Audit fields:
  - createdBy/updatedBy/canceledBy/postedBy/etc.
    should be set in services or subscribers consistently.
end note

note bottom
  Suggested implementation steps:

  1. Add StatusHistory entity, enum and repository.
  2. Add StatusHistoryService::record().
  3. Update Order/Purchase status transition services.
  4. Later update InventoryDocument, ProductionOrder and Payment services.
  5. Add reusable Twig component for status timeline.
  6. Add tests that transition services always write history.
end note

@enduml
